that big, in an authentic kind of way.

451
00:34:38.800 --> 00:34:40.920
And the American Music Award goes to...

452
00:34:41.320 --> 00:34:42.719
Avicii!

453
00:34:53.199 --> 00:34:56.840
Um, I just wanna say thank you
to everyone who voted for me,

454
00:34:56.920 --> 00:35:00.280
um, and thank you to my manager, my label.

455
00:35:00.760 --> 00:35:02.160
Um, thank you so much.

456
00:35:10.760 --> 00:35:13.440
I recovered
from my first kind of pancreatitis.

457
00:35:13.520 --> 00:35:15.640
I was off the pain medication.

458
00:35:15.720 --> 00:35:19.560
Everything was fine,
I w-wasn't on any medication.

459
00:35:21.280 --> 00:35:23.960
- Then I got back to...
- See you tomorrow, man.

460
00:35:24.800 --> 00:35:26.840
...uh, Miami for the Ultra show.

461
00:35:31.520 --> 00:35:35.200
My appendix ruptured
and my, uh, gall bladder ruptured as well.

462
00:35:39.520 --> 00:35:41.000
I need to get some sleep.

463
00:35:41.680 --> 00:35:46.800
I was feeling like shit, and then
the only solution that I got was...

464
00:35:48.280 --> 00:35:51.720
Uh, when-- when does
my next pain medication come?

465
00:35:51.800 --> 00:35:52.840
I have here...

466
00:35:52.920 --> 00:35:56.480
...to take, like, a medicine for it
or to battle through it.

467
00:35:57.040 --> 00:35:59.960
Every time I went into the hospital,
it was like that.

468
00:36:00.040 --> 00:36:02.480
Take this and you'll kind of feel better.

469
00:36:02.560 --> 00:36:05.240
Maybe you're just used
to taking the Percocet?

470
00:36:05.320 --> 00:36:07.000
You've built up a tolerance.

471
00:36:07.680 --> 00:36:10.600
But I've never used--
I've never taken Percocet before.

472
00:36:10.680 --> 00:36:13.720
Percocet is fucking heroin!

473
00:36:13.800 --> 00:36:17.440
- You're getting Percocets?
- Yes, we are, but they're not helping.

474
00:36:17.520 --> 00:36:19.320
Well, yeah, they will...

475
00:36:19.400 --> 00:36:22.240
It didn't help my pain,
that was the weird thing.

476
00:36:22.320 --> 00:36:25.720
So he gave me something
that didn't really help with my pain,

477
00:36:25.800 --> 00:36:28.600
but if the doctor says so,
I guess this is hospital,

478
00:36:28.680 --> 00:36:32.800
I guess he still knows what he's doing
and, you know, kind of like that.

479
00:36:32.880 --> 00:36:35.600
What happened was, uh,
your blood pressure started dropping.

480
00:36:35.680 --> 00:36:40.400
But it started dropping when I started
to add the-- all the other things into it,

481
00:36:40.480 --> 00:36:45.520
when I started adding the, uh,
the anti-anxiety thing for headache,

482
00:36:46.280 --> 00:36:48.200
and the other headache things,

483
00:36:48.720 --> 00:36:52.040
which I would be fine
to try to take everything else off,

484
00:36:52.480 --> 00:36:55.080
but don't take the only things
that are working...

485
00:36:55.160 --> 00:36:56.360
- All right.
- ...for me.

486
00:36:56.440 --> 00:36:58.120
This doesn't feel right.

487
00:36:58.200 --> 00:37:02.560
These pains could last for a very long
time, that was the fucked-up part of it.

488
00:37:03.200 --> 00:37:07.560
I understood when I was in--
When I had my pancreatitis, that it...

489
00:37:08.520 --> 00:37:10.480
I had to be on the medications...

490
00:37:11.640 --> 00:37:15.040
during that, when I was in the hospital,
when I was hospitalised.

491
00:37:15.520 --> 00:37:17.640
That wasn't really the big problem.

492
00:37:18.160 --> 00:37:22.120
The big problem is... that the pain...

493
00:37:23.480 --> 00:37:25.360
the-- the pain stays with you.

494
00:37:27.360 --> 00:37:29.240
For me, it was different each time.

495
00:37:29.320 --> 00:37:32.880
The first time,
it stuck with me for a month.

496
00:37:32.960 --> 00:37:36.280
The second time, I think it stuck with me
for like four months.

497
00:37:36.360 --> 00:37:38.840
It-- It kept not-- It didn't stop.

498
00:37:38.920 --> 00:37:41.520
I di-- I didn't see
the alternatives to this.

499
00:37:42.200 --> 00:37:44.520
You might feel pain free with high doses,

500
00:37:44.600 --> 00:37:47.840
but your body starts--
Your blood pressure starts going down.

501
00:37:47.920 --> 00:37:51.360
But we'll see, we'll try.
If not Dilaudid, something else--

502
00:37:51.440 --> 00:37:54.440
I wasn't even alerted
that my blood pressure was...

503
00:37:54.520 --> 00:37:58.800
There was no communication. No one said:
"Your blood pressure has gone high."

504
00:37:58.880 --> 00:38:01.640
- No, it just--
- It's just being moved and then...

505
00:38:01.720 --> 00:38:03.000
Okay, we'll contact you.

506
00:38:03.080 --> 00:38:04.880
- It's a code blue, okay?
- Okay.

507
00:38:12.400 --> 00:38:15.400
I was on all these kind of medications.

508
00:38:15.480 --> 00:38:18.320
So they were saying:
"You can take this, this is fine.

509
00:38:18.400 --> 00:38:21.760
This is not addictive,
this is not addictive."

510
00:38:21.840 --> 00:38:27.480
And then I was, like, taking
20 pills of some fucking gabapentin here.

511
00:38:27.560 --> 00:38:31.640
All these different medications
that weren't supposed to be addictive.

512
00:38:32.320 --> 00:38:35.240
And it made me feel more anxious.

513
00:38:36.560 --> 00:38:39.400
This kept going
and I started touring again.

514
00:38:41.080 --> 00:38:44.040
Hey, guys, this is Avicii back on Capital.

515
00:38:44.120 --> 00:38:47.880
I think this year is possibly
gonna be bigger than last year.

516
00:38:49.360 --> 00:38:51.720
So I'm really excited, um,
now we're starting

517
00:38:51.800 --> 00:38:56.000
to kind of come into the summer months,
and kind of get back to touring.

518
00:39:07.160 --> 00:39:08.880
One of the hottest acts in music

519
00:39:08.960 --> 00:39:12.840
is coming to New York this weekend
with troubles following on tour.

520
00:39:12.920 --> 00:39:15.560
At the Avicii concert
in Boston last night,

521
00:39:15.640 --> 00:39:18.640
three dozen young people
had to be taken to the hospital,

522
00:39:18.720 --> 00:39:23.320
and many more were treated at the scene
for problems related to drugs and alcohol.

523
00:39:23.400 --> 00:39:27.040
- The thing is, I don't--
- CNN, Fox, CBS releasing reports saying

524
00:39:27.120 --> 00:39:31.080
there's a theme on Avicii concerts
with kids being sent to hospital.

525
00:39:32.080 --> 00:39:34.361
And there was a theme
at Led Zeppelin concerts, too.

526
00:39:34.400 --> 00:39:36.760
Yeah. Yeah, and they brought EDC up.

527
00:39:36.840 --> 00:39:41.200
They're like: "800 people were also sent
to the hospital in EDC,

528
00:39:41.280 --> 00:39:43.280
where Avicii was also performing."

529
00:39:43.360 --> 00:39:47.800
Like I had anything to do...
It was, like, a three-day festival.

530
00:39:47.880 --> 00:39:50.600
- I was one out of 40 people.
- No, no. Here's Tim...

531
00:39:53.800 --> 00:39:57.920
Avicii! Avicii, get a picture
with us. Can we get a picture?

532
00:39:58.000 --> 00:40:01.760
How is it to be you?
How is it to be Avicii?

533
00:40:01.840 --> 00:40:05.440
It's weird. It's weird.
I mean, obviously, I am Avicii,

534
00:40:05.520 --> 00:40:07.360
but then at the same time,

535
00:40:07.440 --> 00:40:13.000
people's perception of who Avicii is
isn't who Tim is.

536
00:40:13.080 --> 00:40:16.760
- I'm a little bit shy.
- Yeah.

537
00:40:16.840 --> 00:40:20.280
I don't really like
being the centre of attention.

538
00:40:20.360 --> 00:40:22.560
But you are. You are, Tim.

539
00:40:22.640 --> 00:40:25.320
Exactly!
But I am. That's-- That's the thing.

540
00:40:25.400 --> 00:40:28.280
That-- That's what makes it so, so weird.

541
00:40:31.360 --> 00:40:33.920
I didn't believe
I could actually slow down.

542
00:40:34.360 --> 00:40:37.920
I didn't believe that I could tour
any differently than this.

543
00:40:39.800 --> 00:40:44.920
I also looked around and I saw
everyone else doing what I was doing,

544
00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:48.040
and they were doing fine,
you know, seemingly.

545
00:40:48.120 --> 00:40:52.360
I know I-I can't read minds,
but they looked like they were doing fine.

546
00:40:52.440 --> 00:40:56.680
Then I started to feel... I mean,
I started to feel crazy, in a sense.

547
00:40:57.480 --> 00:41:00.920
Everything on the checklist is there,
so I should be happy.

548
00:41:04.480 --> 00:41:09.200
I didn't have time to give myself
to properly stop.

549
00:41:09.640 --> 00:41:13.040
What I should have done, obviously,
is to fucking stop,

550
00:41:13.120 --> 00:41:16.320
take four months,
five months, half a year,

551
00:41:17.360 --> 00:41:19.160
recover from...

552
00:41:21.160 --> 00:41:24.440
recover from
not just the pain medicine,

553
00:41:24.520 --> 00:41:26.360
but from the fucking illnesses,

554
00:41:27.280 --> 00:41:31.200
recover from all the years of touring,
all the stress.

555
00:41:33.160 --> 00:41:34.680
But I kept going.

556
00:42:14.440 --> 00:42:17.160
After that summer, that wasn't good.

557
00:42:17.240 --> 00:42:19.720
I felt... I felt like shit.

558
00:42:29.960 --> 00:42:33.160
I did a concert the other day
in this tiny bar...

559
00:42:34.360 --> 00:42:36.240
uh, with no crew,

560
00:42:37.040 --> 00:42:40.800
and when I tried to tune my own guitar
on stage, I couldn't do it.

561
00:42:40.880 --> 00:42:42.240
It was so embarrassing.

562
00:42:44.600 --> 00:42:46.960
- It was really embarrassing.
- That's perfect.

563
00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:50.400
It brought it right back
to the beginning.

564
00:42:50.480 --> 00:42:51.320
That's great.

565
00:42:51.400 --> 00:42:54.960
My passion for music was always there,
so I loved making music.

566
00:42:55.040 --> 00:42:57.360
That was the one thing
I could come back to.

567
00:42:57.440 --> 00:43:00.120
- The one above that.
- Yeah, I'm gonna do...

568
00:43:01.480 --> 00:43:03.800
I'd say-- I'd say, maybe one, maybe...

569
00:43:05.720 --> 00:43:07.840
It just does it like a transition thing.

570
00:43:32.960 --> 00:43:34.720
- Do you like it more when it gets...?
- Huh?

571
00:43:34.800 --> 00:43:37.520
Do you like it better when it's,
like, more with the higher...?

572
00:43:37.600 --> 00:43:39.360
You're so talented, man.

573
00:43:39.840 --> 00:43:41.640
- Do you like the synths?
- What?

574
00:43:41.720 --> 00:43:43.760
- Do you like the new synth?
- I love it.

575
00:43:46.600 --> 00:43:47.880
Hoo-hoo-hoo!

576
00:43:47.960 --> 00:43:51.120
♪ Here you come to raise me up ♪

577
00:43:51.200 --> 00:43:54.760
♪ When I'm beaten and broken up ♪

578
00:43:55.360 --> 00:43:59.520
♪ And now I'm back in the arms I love ♪

579
00:44:02.040 --> 00:44:03.440
Really good.

580
00:44:03.520 --> 00:44:05.520
Really good. I've got everything.

581
00:44:08.640 --> 00:44:12.000
Time went on, and I didn't feel better.

582
00:44:12.440 --> 00:44:15.520
And it kept happening,
even though when I went into--

583
00:44:15.600 --> 00:44:18.280
To periods of just
purely taking care of myself,

584
00:44:18.360 --> 00:44:20.760
it kept happening, I kept feeling bad.

585
00:44:20.840 --> 00:44:23.720
And my body kept feeling bad.

586
00:44:32.120 --> 00:44:34.040
There was never an end of shows.

587
00:44:34.680 --> 00:44:38.160
Even when I really felt like
I was gonna hit a wall or something,

588
00:44:38.240 --> 00:44:43.440
I gave myself a couple of months just to
kind of relax and-- and not do anything.

589
00:44:43.520 --> 00:44:48.000
And even in those months,
I couldn't get myself to relax,

590
00:44:48.080 --> 00:44:52.600
because my mind was still focused on
when I was gonna start up touring again.

591
00:45:27.960 --> 00:45:29.000
Mm.

592
00:45:31.440 --> 00:45:33.440
Mm.

593
00:45:47.240 --> 00:45:48.840
In the beginning of the year,

594
00:45:48.920 --> 00:45:52.000
I get presented with all the shows
of the upcoming year,

595
00:45:52.360 --> 00:45:55.400
and I have to say
which I want to do and which I don't.

596
00:45:55.480 --> 00:45:58.680
And then, along the lines of the year,
stuff pumps up.

597
00:45:58.760 --> 00:46:01.680
You know, my manager might want
to push something in,

598
00:46:01.760 --> 00:46:03.640
someone else might want
to push something in,

599
00:46:03.720 --> 00:46:08.200
then is pushing my manager to push it in.
I might want to push something in.

600
00:46:08.280 --> 00:46:13.480
You know, all these things kind of come in
and they cause a shit ton of stress.

601
00:46:18.600 --> 00:46:21.200
Tim decides to rent a big, giant villa.

602
00:46:21.280 --> 00:46:25.640
He's, like, using this as his base,
flying out all over Europe doing shows.

603
00:46:27.800 --> 00:46:32.160
He was touring, I think it was
three or four times per week.

604
00:46:34.840 --> 00:46:38.720
And, uh, he was working on,
uh, his second album as well.

605
00:46:57.640 --> 00:47:01.760
Even though the shows got harder
to do, the touring got harder to do,

606
00:47:01.840 --> 00:47:03.600
there were always moments,

607
00:47:03.680 --> 00:47:06.080
during the touring moments,
during the shows,

608
00:47:06.160 --> 00:47:09.040
when I could find a genuine happiness
from music.

609
00:47:16.240 --> 00:47:20.320
To be able to do the music or,
uh, to be able to go out for the touring,

610
00:47:20.400 --> 00:47:22.080
he was taking medication.

611
00:47:22.160 --> 00:47:23.680
By this time, Tim was--

612
00:47:23.760 --> 00:47:27.720
He was supposed to, like, be over
all, uh, the medicines and stuff.

613
00:47:28.880 --> 00:47:31.920
I went to psychiatrists,
I went to doctors.

614
00:47:32.280 --> 00:47:35.280
I tried so many different diets.

615
00:47:37.200 --> 00:47:40.800
You know, we-- I even changed--
I changed the way I toured,

616
00:47:40.880 --> 00:47:44.320
not enough at all,
but I changed it,

617
00:47:44.400 --> 00:47:46.720
and I-I thought I did enough, you know.

618
00:47:52.840 --> 00:47:55.680
But by my standards,
that was a chilled schedule.

619
00:47:56.120 --> 00:47:59.360
But then the other five days
was working on the album.

620
00:48:07.360 --> 00:48:13.240
When you start, you just wanna make...
cool beats and have fun, you know?

621
00:48:13.320 --> 00:48:16.680
You're not thinking like:
"Oh, I need to have a hit record."

622
00:48:16.760 --> 00:48:20.800
You make those cool beats, you have fun,
you wanna play those-- those beats,

623
00:48:20.880 --> 00:48:25.160
and then, it's just positivity,
it's just fun, it's just entertainment,

624
00:48:26.080 --> 00:48:27.440
and sharing your love.

625
00:48:28.160 --> 00:48:33.880
But then, after, when you had, like,
let's say, three massive global hits,

626
00:48:34.520 --> 00:48:38.280
everybody expects you
to come every time with a global hit,

627
00:48:38.360 --> 00:48:40.080
and this is really hard.

628
00:48:41.960 --> 00:48:44.280
I've been working on Stories for forever.

629
00:48:44.360 --> 00:48:48.600
In-- In my time schedule, it was forever,
because it had taken two years,

630
00:48:48.680 --> 00:48:53.360
and, I mean, the first album took me
three months to make the majority of it,

631
00:48:53.440 --> 00:48:55.800
and this was a completely different thing.

632
00:49:23.960 --> 00:49:26.040
Yeah! Yeah!

633
00:49:52.120 --> 00:49:55.680
He's just like a shell
of what he used to be.

634
00:49:55.760 --> 00:49:59.800
The guy I used to know
wasn't really there anymore.

635
00:50:04.160 --> 00:50:08.360
It was so over the top,
'cause I wasn't drinking when I woke up.

636
00:50:08.440 --> 00:50:10.920
I wasn't-- Y-- I didn't...

637
00:50:12.160 --> 00:50:16.320
I know all my ideas
of a problem wasn't there.

638
00:50:16.920 --> 00:50:21.840
So it didn't-- I couldn't connect
my problem with my lifestyle.

639
00:50:24.120 --> 00:50:30.920
Finally, when the album was done, he, uh,
he had to do this, uh, promotion tour.

640
00:50:31.320 --> 00:50:33.000
Hey, guys, this is Avicii.

641
00:50:33.080 --> 00:50:36.800
Follow my profile to get updates
from my latest album, Stories.

642
00:50:37.360 --> 00:50:38.440
Hey, everybody...

643
00:50:39.640 --> 00:50:43.360
Hey, everybody, it's Avicii.
Check out my new single...

644
00:50:52.200 --> 00:50:53.200
Mm?

645
00:50:55.080 --> 00:50:56.960
"Insert artist's name."

646
00:51:20.240 --> 00:51:23.800
The best thing about falling
is getting up.

647
00:51:24.680 --> 00:51:27.040
A-And the fact is, Tim is up.

648
00:51:27.120 --> 00:51:31.480
When we were finished with
the therapy, Tim wanted to go to the U.S.

649
00:51:36.240 --> 00:51:40.000
Early morning, like four o'clock
in the morning, we got on the plane.

650
00:51:47.560 --> 00:51:49.880
We start flying over Los Angeles.

651
00:51:50.960 --> 00:51:52.320
Wow, this is awesome.

652
00:51:54.760 --> 00:51:58.920
We get in the cars
and we drive towards Malibu.

653
00:52:07.440 --> 00:52:11.080
And we kind of arrive
at this insane house.

654
00:52:14.440 --> 00:52:16.960
Right by the beach, green grass.

655
00:52:19.440 --> 00:52:21.800
We come down and we see the sunset,

656
00:52:21.880 --> 00:52:26.560
this beautiful Malibu sunset,
and we're like: "Wow!"

657
00:52:36.640 --> 00:52:38.880
We met up in Malibu again.

658
00:52:41.560 --> 00:52:45.720
You could tell that he-- he had been
working on-- on himself a lot.

659
00:52:48.480 --> 00:52:49.960
He was a lot different.

660
00:52:51.560 --> 00:52:53.640
He was determined to change his life.

661
00:52:56.920 --> 00:53:00.680
We built a studio
with the most amazing view ever.

662
00:53:01.440 --> 00:53:03.800
We really took out the best in each other.

663
00:53:03.880 --> 00:53:08.320
We started kind of figuring out
how we were gonna plan this and that.

664
00:53:08.400 --> 00:53:11.440
We shut off Tim's e-mail,
we shut off his phone.

665
00:53:12.200 --> 00:53:14.720
That was a really good time for him.

666
00:53:16.440 --> 00:53:19.160
It was a very, very, very nice period.

667
00:54:11.160 --> 00:54:15.600
I felt a lot more collected and I thought:
"I've taken my time now, gone to therapy.

668
00:54:15.680 --> 00:54:18.800
I've been through this and this.
I feel a shit ton better."

669
00:54:18.880 --> 00:54:21.280
And I wanted to get started
on my new album,

670
00:54:21.360 --> 00:54:23.960
so I got a bunch
of my songwriting friends.

671
00:54:24.040 --> 00:54:28.360
We decided to go from L.A. to Miami
on a bus and stop on different places

672
00:54:28.440 --> 00:54:33.840
and kind of do some sort of
outdoor awesomeness studio

673
00:54:33.920 --> 00:54:36.720
in the most kind of epic settings
you could think of.

674
00:56:16.080 --> 00:56:17.080
Mm.

675
00:57:39.880 --> 00:57:43.920
My heart is beating. I can't see clear.

676
00:57:44.000 --> 00:57:47.160
♪ My heart is beating, I can't see clear ♪

677
00:57:49.640 --> 00:57:51.120
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

678
00:58:42.200 --> 00:58:43.200
Nice.

679
00:59:00.200 --> 00:59:03.200
I was like:
"Wow, this is gonna be so great."

680
00:59:04.120 --> 00:59:08.440
And then... the road trip ends in Miami.

681
00:59:11.560 --> 00:59:16.280
And the Ultra gig is... is happening.

682
00:59:22.240 --> 00:59:25.960
There was something wrong
with the computer before the show.

683
00:59:30.040 --> 00:59:32.400
- Can I have a picture with him?
- Not now.

684
00:59:32.480 --> 00:59:34.280
- No?
- No way. Sorry. No, no way.

685
00:59:36.880 --> 00:59:37.880
Yeah, I'm here.

686
00:59:41.000 --> 00:59:41.840
Yeah, sure.

687
00:59:43.880 --> 00:59:46.480
I'll start getting more and more nervous.

688
00:59:47.960 --> 00:59:50.600
Things are becoming closer to the show.

689
00:59:51.440 --> 00:59:56.040
Someone comes and tells me: "Okay,
now it's time. It's like five minutes to."

690
00:59:56.120 --> 00:59:57.920
So I'm like: "All right, fuck it."

691
01:00:23.760 --> 01:00:24.760
Okay.

692
01:00:33.040 --> 01:00:37.320
- Sorry. Can I take a picture?
- No, no, no, not now. Not now.

693
01:00:47.200 --> 01:00:50.560
Like, he was pushing himself
for, like, every single day

694
01:00:50.640 --> 01:00:52.680
for whatever how long this was,

695
01:00:53.760 --> 01:00:58.200
and it felt like it was a ticking bomb
and it just exploded at a show.

696
01:01:20.960 --> 01:01:24.520
I thought the other one was great.
There were two tracks...

697
01:01:36.160 --> 01:01:38.520
I see you. I see you out there...

698
01:01:49.960 --> 01:01:53.240
You good? Okay,
I'll be stage right if you need anything.

699
01:02:11.680 --> 01:02:15.080
I'd been away for-- for--
It's eight months, six months.

700
01:02:15.160 --> 01:02:18.240
Now, I've-- I've literally done
everything I can.

701
01:02:23.040 --> 01:02:28.920
And straight away,
I still... I still get stressed out.

702
01:02:29.000 --> 01:02:32.000
I still don't like this.

703
01:02:54.920 --> 01:02:57.080
Thank you to all artists

704
01:02:57.520 --> 01:03:03.640
who've helped me develop
musically and personally.

705
01:03:06.560 --> 01:03:10.000
Thank you, Semi Badreddine,
for all your personal support, talks,

706
01:03:10.080 --> 01:03:11.320
and helping me growing up.

707
01:03:11.400 --> 01:03:15.200
I have a feeling I'd be dead if not
for you, and I will always love you.

708
01:03:46.280 --> 01:03:50.280
And last but not least, a thank you to
every fan who's ever bought a ticket,

709
01:03:50.360 --> 01:03:51.600
or snuck in...

710
01:03:53.360 --> 01:03:56.320
...bought a song or downloaded it,
loved...

711
01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:04.640
It's your thoughts and ideas
about the music that helped me evolve,

712
01:04:04.720 --> 01:04:08.240
and I do owe everything I have to you.

713
01:04:08.320 --> 01:04:11.280
Special thanks to everyone who's...

714
01:04:12.640 --> 01:04:17.520
been a part of the team since day one.

715
01:04:20.720 --> 01:04:23.160
Our journey is far from finished.

716
01:06:01.480 --> 01:06:03.240
I felt shitty, I felt terrible,

717
01:06:03.320 --> 01:06:07.360
because I saw how-- how happy all
the fans are, and I don't fucking like it.

718
01:06:07.440 --> 01:06:11.600
I'm standing up there, pretending
I like something that I don't like doing.

719
01:06:11.680 --> 01:06:15.200
That-- That was just it for me,
because I just knew that there's--

720
01:06:15.280 --> 01:06:18.920
I can't see a way for me to do this
and be happy about it.

721
01:06:19.280 --> 01:06:21.600
After that, I just decided:
"Fuck, I'm gonna quit."

722
01:06:25.520 --> 01:06:28.520
- I think I'm gonna cry.
- We are very sad.

723
01:06:28.600 --> 01:06:30.640
It's unfair, Avicii. Unfair.

724
01:06:30.720 --> 01:06:34.440
Dance music D.J. Avicii
officially retires from touring.

725
01:06:42.760 --> 01:06:43.760
Very sad.

726
01:06:44.480 --> 01:06:48.760
He stands out above anyone else,
and that's why it's so sad to see him go.

727
01:06:48.840 --> 01:06:54.840
It's been a great five years, good music,
and, you know, jam after jam, nice tracks.

728
01:06:54.920 --> 01:06:57.320
If this is what he has to do,
then so be it.

729
01:06:57.400 --> 01:06:59.200
In a letter posted on his website,

730
01:06:59.280 --> 01:07:01.080
Avicii told followers he would:

731
01:07:01.160 --> 01:07:03.320
"Continue to speak to fans
in his music."

732
01:07:03.400 --> 01:07:04.480
♪ Doo-doo-doo... ♪

733
01:08:03.360 --> 01:08:06.800
Tim's life almost revolves around him

734
01:08:06.880 --> 01:08:10.520
being able to create his own music.

735
01:08:10.600 --> 01:08:14.880
Was he doing that part
to get to the concert,

736
01:08:14.960 --> 01:08:18.960
or was he doing it because
he actually just loved making the music?

737
01:08:19.439 --> 01:08:21.240
I think he loved making the music.

738
01:10:14.480 --> 01:10:15.480
Yup.

739
01:10:17.520 --> 01:10:21.240
...Legos.
Our homes and lives are infused with

740
01:10:21.880 --> 01:10:24.400
Scandinavian furniture and design.

741
01:10:25.120 --> 01:10:27.480
Um, some of us dance and sing

742
01:10:27.560 --> 01:10:29.400
to Abba and Avicii.

743
01:10:43.480 --> 01:10:44.480
Hee-hee!

744
01:10:56.000 --> 01:10:58.920
Even though he decided
to quit with the touring,

745
01:10:59.000 --> 01:11:00.840
he still had a lot of shows to do,

746
01:11:00.920 --> 01:11:03.960
so he had the whole summer
that he had to tour still.

747
01:11:04.040 --> 01:11:05.640
He had to do Ibiza.

748
01:11:05.720 --> 01:11:11.920
He had to do all these places in-- around
Europe and he started with-- with Vegas.

749
01:13:24.680 --> 01:13:26.200
Mm.

750
01:14:38.880 --> 01:14:42.840
He, uh, he went to speak with
who is the owner of the hotel,

751
01:14:42.920 --> 01:14:44.400
together with Steve Wynn.

752
01:14:45.240 --> 01:14:46.680
Mr. President.

753
01:15:12.960 --> 01:15:13.960
Mm-hmm.

754
01:15:23.120 --> 01:15:26.680
They had a great talk
and understood completely,

755
01:15:26.760 --> 01:15:29.480
and, uh, that was,
uh, it with the Vegas shows.

756
01:15:39.720 --> 01:15:41.720
When I decided to stop...

757
01:15:43.000 --> 01:15:45.600
I was expecting a completely different...

758
01:15:46.280 --> 01:15:49.240
I was expecting support in stopping.

759
01:15:49.320 --> 01:15:52.360
I was expecting to,
especially with what I'd been through.

760
01:15:52.440 --> 01:15:53.440
And I'd been very open

761
01:15:53.520 --> 01:15:56.920
with every-- everyone I worked with
and everyone who knows me.

762
01:15:57.000 --> 01:16:00.720
I've been very open with what
I've been through, what I've felt, and...

763
01:16:00.800 --> 01:16:01.840
what I've done.

764
01:16:01.920 --> 01:16:03.480
You know, everyone knows,

765
01:16:04.000 --> 01:16:08.520
uh, that I've been anxious and, you know,
everything, and that I've been trying.

766
01:16:08.600 --> 01:16:12.640
So I-I... I didn't expect people to try

767
01:16:12.720 --> 01:16:15.920
to push me to-- to do more shows,

768
01:16:17.040 --> 01:16:18.360
when it really...

769
01:16:22.440 --> 01:16:26.360
When they'd seen
how shitty I felt... doing it.

770
01:16:26.440 --> 01:16:31.240
So-- So I did get a lot of resistance
when I wanted to stop doing the shows.

771
01:16:36.640 --> 01:16:37.800
Yeah!

772
01:16:43.080 --> 01:16:44.080
Liam!

773
01:17:31.640 --> 01:17:36.000
Anyone that-- that goes
from-- from being in school

774
01:17:36.840 --> 01:17:40.720
to all-- to having a career
and being successful

775
01:17:40.800 --> 01:17:43.040
misses a big part of growing up.

776
01:18:14.480 --> 01:18:17.840
Obviously that comes with challenges.
He doesn't-- You know, there's a...

777
01:19:42.000 --> 01:19:43.000
What's your name?

778
01:19:45.200 --> 01:19:47.160
- Tim.
- Nice to meet you.

779
01:19:47.240 --> 01:19:49.800
One, two, three.

780
01:20:19.400 --> 01:20:21.400
I'm so happy I'm finally here.

781
01:20:24.560 --> 01:20:27.800
I've had the best five days
in Japan ever.

782
01:20:28.960 --> 01:20:31.920
You guys have
the most beautiful country ever.

783
01:26:37.880 --> 01:26:39.120
Hm? Yeah, sure.

784
01:28:21.840 --> 01:28:22.840
Move.

785
01:29:17.400 --> 01:29:22.000
Avicii! Avicii! Avicii!

786
01:29:22.400 --> 01:29:25.720
Avicii! Avicii...

787
01:30:17.920 --> 01:30:18.920
Ushuaia.

788
01:30:20.760 --> 01:30:23.400
Thank you so much for tonight.

789
01:30:23.480 --> 01:30:25.640
Avicii! Avicii...

790
01:30:26.360 --> 01:30:29.240
I couldn't have asked
for a-- a better last show.

791
01:30:31.200 --> 01:30:33.720
Thank you so much for tonight,
you were awesome.

792
01:31:55.760 --> 01:31:58.440
The-- The performance part of it

793
01:31:58.840 --> 01:32:03.200
is one part of the artistic arc.

794
01:32:03.680 --> 01:32:05.520
And if you cut that out of it,

795
01:32:06.440 --> 01:32:09.280
you still have the life
of the creative composer,

796
01:32:09.720 --> 01:32:11.640
the person who puts it all together.

797
01:32:11.720 --> 01:32:16.960
That is a beautiful,
wonderful, rewarding life.

798
01:32:19.280 --> 01:32:23.040
I watched his ups
and I watched his downs,

799
01:32:23.400 --> 01:32:25.520
and I can understand that because...

800
01:32:26.600 --> 01:32:31.040
you know, I too had success
at a very, very young age.

801
01:32:31.120 --> 01:32:34.640
So, it's hard for people
who don't have success

802
01:32:35.000 --> 01:32:40.000
in their twenties to understand
what comes with,

803
01:32:40.560 --> 01:32:44.920
you know, anything you want to buy in
your twenties, anything you want to have.

804
01:32:45.000 --> 01:32:48.680
And then you're gonna have, like, a gang
of leeches, you know what I'm saying?

805
01:32:48.760 --> 01:32:53.960
Then you got people who just gonna just
try to suck you up, you know what I mean?

806
01:32:54.040 --> 01:32:56.200
And now, you know,
it's almost like sometimes

807
01:32:56.280 --> 01:32:59.000
you feel like you in a world
all by yourself.

808
01:32:59.360 --> 01:33:05.800
So, for you to find a way out of that
and to still say: "You know what?

809
01:33:07.240 --> 01:33:13.360
I'm Tim, I love music, but you know what,
right now, I just need to find myself."

810
01:33:22.840 --> 01:33:26.560
But now it's only been
a month since I did my last show

811
01:33:26.640 --> 01:33:27.640
and I feel...

812
01:33:29.960 --> 01:33:35.640
I mean, like, I feel like
I did when I was like 18, maybe.

813
01:33:36.200 --> 01:33:41.160
I feel I'm in the same
kind of spirit as I was then.

814
01:34:01.480 --> 01:34:04.640
I started making music
and I started DJing.

815
01:34:04.720 --> 01:34:08.560
I just quit my job
and I don't really have a plan yet.
